  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data exploration (kibana_sample_data_logs)**\n- 14,074 requests, all from `geo.src` US, across 4 hosts and 448 distinct URLs. Average response is about 5.7 KB.\n- Response codes: 200 (12,832), 404 (801), 503 (441). The only 5xx code is 503.\n- The timestamps run from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03, which is after today's date (2026-10-12). I set the dashboard's time range to 2026-09-01 through 2026-12-31 so the data shows up.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-da93891c Web logs overview\"**\n- Dashboard ID: `eff-da93891c-web-logs-overview-626c4775701f`\n- Panels:\n  - Total requests (metric, count)\n  - Average response size in bytes (metric)\n  - Requests over time (line, date histogram)\n  - Requests by response code (pie, terms on `response.keyword`)\n  - 5xx responses (ES|QL metric, `response.keyword LIKE \"5*\"`)\n  - Top URLs by requests (ES|QL table, with request count and average bytes)\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-da93891c 5xx spike\"**\n- Rule ID: `7da2f288-9f7a-4000-896e-ec41cbd3082a`, type `.es-query`, consumer `stackAlerts`, status enabled.\n- Runs every 1m. Counts documents where `response.keyword` matches `5*` in the last 5 minutes, and fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- The rule's window is relative to the current time. Because the sample data's timestamps are in the future, the rule will not match anything yet.\n\nI didn't add any connectors, so the rule has no notification action. It will record firings in the alert list but won't send anything.",
